      "title": "A homage to Hokusai",
      "description": "If you’ve seen a popular artwork depicting Mt. Fuji, it is most likely by the Japanese ukiyo-e artist Hokusai. His series of landscape prints titled Thirty-six Views of Mount Fuji are one of the most recognizable work of Japanese art, and have influenced several art movements, including Impressionism.",
